{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>הרינו חלנו.</b> [We conceived, we writhed]: רוח, and likewise ילדנו, and the meaning is that we had no power to escape, and these are [deliverances that were not made]; we cannot do:" "<b>ארץ.</b> [In] the land, defective bet, like כי ששת ימים (Exodus 20:11):" "<b>ובל יפלו.</b> Some say it is deficient alef, as in ויפלו מאד בעיניהם (Nehemiah 6:16), but ויפלו there means only what it sounds like, as I will explain. In my opinion: שלא נוכל שלא יפלו:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The bracketed phrase בל נעשה appears corrupt or truncated; translated hyper-literally. The antecedent of the final 'we cannot do' is uncertain.", 1 "Ibn Ezra identifies ארץ as a construct form missing the prefixed bet; rendered his term 'חסר בית' as 'defective bet.'", 2 "The final clause שלא נוכל שלא יפלו is syntactically compressed (lit. 'that we cannot [fail to] / they will not fall'); left cryptic as in the original."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:20.657057399Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}